[COMMENTS]
STATION,Velocity area station with Crump profile flat V weir. Natural flow regime. GENERAL: Velocity area station, initially with a gravel shoal control. Improved in 1977 by installing a 25m wide Crump profile Flat V weir. STATION HYDROMETRY: Weir rebuilt in September 1994, and recapped in October 1995. Cableway spans 44m. Above approx. 3m the rb floodplain is inundated. A major event in October 1998 altered the shape of the channel at low flows. Multiple peak flow ratings applied across period of record. Gaugings fit well to respective ratings. FLOW RECORD: Weir rebuilt between 31/8/94 and 7/9/94, no data available. Full period of record peak flow data reviewed and released in September 2019 (WINFAP Files v8). Rating reviewed in 2022 and data reprocessed for the full period of record. FLOW REGIME: Natural to within 10% at Q95.
CATCHMENT,Natural catchment. Headwaters drain the very wet Tywi Forest, underlain by indurated Ordovician sediments. The middle and lower reaches are on relatively more permeable Silurian rocks, but generally a responsive catchment of very low permeability. Predominantly upland pasture (mainly grassland) but with some forested areas, mainly in western headwaters.
Qmed Suitability,Gauged above QMED. Good fit to ratings.
Pooling Suitability,Few high flow gaugings. Rating cannot be validated beyond QMED.
[END]
